      "writtenOn": "2021-05-02T05:35:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we need to go up 2 levels on the driver. What I mean by this is that this driver is for the named-cbi-ssfc-value meaning the grandchild of named-cbi-ssfc. I\u0027m not a fan of having to depend on the node name in the driver. I\u0027m wondering if we set DT_DRV_COMPAT to named_cbi_ssfc and created one instance of the driver for that root node.\n\nIf we want to enforce that there can be only one instance of it, I believe we can do that with DT_NUM_INST_STATUS_OKAY and make sure that the value is \u003c 2.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "d6b66ddecd54a03ef99553cf950bf2677f3449a3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4f2302ba_68fe4400",
