      "writtenOn": "2021-05-02T05:35:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have an alternate suggestion to this. What if we have an enum that we create using each node\u0027s ID (effectively, similar to what you did with CBI_SSFC_UNION_ENTRY_NAME, but it would need to iterate through the children).\n\nThis would look like:\n\nenum cbi_ssfc_names {\n#ifdef DT_NODE_EXISTS(CBI_SSFC_NODE)\n  DT_FOREACH_CHILD(CBI_SSFC_NODE, CBI_SSFC_NAME_WITH_COMMA)\n#endif\n  CBI_SSFC_SIZE,\n};\n\nYou can still do your build assert to check that CBI_SSFC_SIZE \u003c\u003d 32.\n\nNow you can use the enum value 0-31 with the BIT(CBI_SSFC_NAME(node_id)) to get the bitfield. This would do away with the `size` field.\n\nThe enum values you would have from above would look like (simplified to avoid the full path generated by devicetree):\n\nCBI_SSFC_base_sensor_bmi160,\nCBI_SSFC_lid_sensor_bma255,\nCBI_SSFC_lightbar_10_led,\n\nWhat I\u0027m assuming is that we don\u0027t have a hard requirement for the base sensor to have 3 bits in the bitfield. It should just have enough for the children I assume.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 117,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 125,
        "endChar": 2
      },
